# Line endings for the files where they are load-bearing.
#
# Deliberately narrow. A blanket `* text=auto` is the right long-term answer, but
# adding it here would renormalise most of the tree in one commit and bury this
# refactor's diff, so it is left for its own change.
#
# These two paths must stay byte-identical: the dashboard export inlines the
# backend copy, the page loads the frontend one, and
# backend/tests/test_dashboard_export.py asserts they match. They are the same
# bytes today, but the invariant currently holds only because both happen to get
# the same treatment from whatever core.autocrlf is set to locally. Pinning both
# to LF makes that explicit rather than incidental -- a checkout that produced CRLF
# for one and LF for the other would fail the suite for a reason nobody would
# think to look for.
backend/vanna/dashboards/vendor/tile-figure.js  text eol=lf
frontend/public/assets/shared/tile-figure.js    text eol=lf

# Generated SQL, replayed by psql. Kept LF so a diff after regenerating shows only
# what actually changed -- a whole-file line-ending flip hides the real edit.
database/migrations/*.sql   text eol=lf
database/seed/*.sql         text eol=lf
database/sql_schema.sql     text eol=lf

# Semantic manifests and their build output. `projects/demo` and `projects/chinook`
# once differed by nothing but CRLF, which is how a byte-for-byte duplicate went
# unnoticed long enough to make nine tables invisible.
backend/projects/**/*.yml   text eol=lf
backend/projects/**/*.json  text eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png   binary
*.webp  binary
*.mp4   binary
*.webm  binary
*.ico   binary
